## The PCI ID database

`src/lsdsk/adapters/hw/decode/pci.ids.gz` is a compressed, trimmed copy of
`pci.ids` from the PCI ID Project, https://pci-ids.ucw.cz/, maintained by
Albert Pool, Martin Mares and other volunteers.

Upstream offers it under either the GNU General Public License version 2 or
later, or the 3-clause BSD License. lsdsk redistributes it under the 3-clause
BSD License. The copy keeps upstream's own comment header, which carries that
statement and the version date of the snapshot.

It is trimmed to the vendor and device lines lsdsk reads. The subsystem lines
and the device class section are dropped; no name is altered.

lsdsk uses it to name a controller the same way whatever the machine is. Where
the operating system ships its own `pci.ids`, that one is preferred, because a
distribution refreshes it more often than lsdsk is released.

